examples.question_text:
The point $P(2,3)$ lies on $y=f(x)$. Find and label its corresponding point on each graph.
(a) $y=-f(x)$
(b) $y=f(-x)$
(c) $y=-f(-x)$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[<->,black] (-3.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4)--(0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[black] (2,3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,3) node[above right] {$P(2,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
(a) Keep $x$ and negate $y$: $Q(2,-3)$.
(b) Negate $x$ and keep $y$: $R(-2,3)$.
(c) Negate both coordinates: $S(-2,-3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{reflectionblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-3.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-4)--(0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[black] (2,3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,3) node[above right] {$P(2,3)$};
\fill[reflectionblue] (2,-3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,-3) node[below right,text=reflectionblue] {$Q(2,-3)$};
\fill[reflectionblue] (-2,3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,3) node[above left,text=reflectionblue] {$R(-2,3)$};
\fill[reflectionblue] (-2,-3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,-3) node[below left,text=reflectionblue] {$S(-2,-3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
